  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad arbetsmarknadsinformation Tanzania</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Labour Market Information - Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsens syfte &#xe4;r att bidra till f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad arbetsmarknadsinformation och b&#xe4;ttre fungerande arbetsmarknader i Tanzania. 
Det svenska st&#xf6;det till Arbetsf&#xf6;rmedlingen ska st&#xe4;rka kapaciteten hos Tanzaniska arbetsf&#xf6;rmedlingen TaESA och Arbetsmarknadsministeriet (PMO-LYED) i att insamla, analysera och disseminera arbetsmarknadsinformation och i slut&#xe4;ndan bidra till &#xf6;kad produktiv syssels&#xe4;ttning, framf&#xf6;r allt f&#xf6;r unga kvinnor och m&#xe4;n i Tanzania.  
Programmet skall implementeras genom samarbete med svenska arbetsf&#xf6;rmedlingen, TaESA och PMO-LYED. &#xc4;ven andra akt&#xf6;rer s&#xe5;som utbildningsministeriet, arbetsgivarorganisationer, privata sektorn, nationella statistikbyr&#xe5;n och ungdomsorganisationer kommer bidra till programmets genomf&#xf6;rande.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of the contribution is to support improved labor market information and better functioning of labor markets in Tanzania.
The Swedish support to the Employment Agency will contribute to strengthening the capacity of the Tanzanian employment agency TaESA and the Ministry of Labour(PMO-LYED) to collect, analyze and disseminate labor market information and ultimately contribute to increased productive employment, especially for young women and men in Tanzania.
The program will be implemented through cooperation with the Swedish Employment Service, TaESA and PMO-LYED. Other actors such as the Ministry of Education, employers&apos; organizations, the private sector, national statistics and youth organizations will contribute to the implementation of the program.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The expected project outcomes are: 1. Strengthened capacity at PMO-LYED and TaESA on labour market information, analysis and forecasting leading to better adapted education and vocational training in relation to the needs of the labour market
2. Strengthened capacity and cooperation between PMO-LYED, TaESA, MoEST and NGOs on guidance and communication of labour market information to youth, leading to better informed youth, students as well as unemployed youth.</narrative>
  </description>
